# The help system and the pagers.

shot    help
cap     The help system answering a topic.  It keeps a .hlp file and an
cap     index per subject in SYS/HELP, offers what it has at the `Topic ?'
cap     prompt, and pages the article.  It is asked for by path because
cap     bash has a `help' builtin of its own, and the builtin wins: typing
cap     `help' alone never reaches this program.
run     /dd/CMDS/help
wait    5
send    space\r
wait    6

shot    helpindex
for     helpindex lessecho lesskey rdoc
cap     helpindex builds the index the help system reads; lesskey compiles
cap     a key-binding file for less.
run     helpindex -?
wait    8
run     lesskey -?
wait    8

shot    less
cap     less, paging the disk's own documentation.  SYS/less.hlp is here,
cap     so its help screen works.
run     less /dd/DOC/README-RUNNING
wait    5
send    q
wait    2

shot    rdoc
cap     rdoc is Rueckdokumentation -- reverse documentation, from c't in
cap     1988.  Hand it C source and it prints the control structure as an
cap     indented skeleton: every if, else, for, switch and case in place,
cap     with the code between them taken away.  This is the tail of what it
cap     makes of keep.c.
run     rdoc /dd/SRC/keep/keep.c | tail -l=20
wait    90
